          "criterion": "paraphrase_fidelity",
          "location": "common_traps[11].text",
          "problem": "The trap says the bar on dispensing expired product 'comes from 247 CMR 9.01(12)' without the paragraph's recipient qualifier. 9.01(12) forbids dispensing or distributing expired, outdated, defective, contaminated, counterfeit, contraband or otherwise substandard drugs to a person or entity not licensed or legally authorized to receive them.",
          "rationale": "orientation[5] quotes the qualifier correctly and calls not dispensing expired product to a patient the safe course. The practical lesson (do not dispense expired stock) is sound and would not mislead a candidate on Massachusetts facts. Only the shortened trap wording attributes a broader flat bar to 9.01(12) than its words state. The observation that 21 U.S.C. 351 and 352 name no expiration ground is literally accurate and hedged ('as a matter of course'). Weighed as Low; no criterion fails.",
